      "message": "fix(motion): normal lines through one point no longer certify an axis\n\nThe axis judgement counted a facet as an inlier when its normal line\nmet the candidate axis. Two-triangle faces anchor their lines at the\nface centre and a single-band wall anchors its lines at the bar's mid\npoint, so a box's faces (or a single-band shaft's wall) meet EVERY line\nthrough that point. A small finely meshed boss or cross hole then\nsupplied the bearings, and the fit trusted a wrong axis: a plate with\nan r5 boss at (10, 0) read a 45-degree axis, a single-band r10 h150\nshaft with a D-flat and a cross hole read X, and (on PR #204) a 60 mm\ncube with an off-centre boss read a tilted axis through its centre.\n\nNew axis_point.rs: find the point the inliers' lines meet best (area\nleast squares, refitted on the area half that misses it least). When\nthe lines through it carry half the inlier area, those facets alone\nmust pass the coarseness gate about the axis - a pencil of lines has no\ndirection of its own and stands for a revolve only when it is itself\nrotationally symmetric about the axis. A single-band CAD cylinder still\nfits; banded walls are untouched. The bearing-gap gate moves into the\nnew module, shared. On an isotropic part a pole (facing-flat) axis is\nno longer tilted by the direction refinement.\n\nPins (each fails on the base 7fff05c):\na_plate_with_a_boss_off_its_centre_line_is_refused_by_name,\na_single_band_shaft_with_a_flat_and_a_cross_hole_is_not_read_across,\na_cube_with_an_off_centre_boss_is_refused_by_name (1 and 5 bands);\na_single_band_bar_still_fits_its_true_axis guards the common export.\n\nFixes #208\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
