  {
    "sha": "e883ae67b158cddd2361ff6968eb65c4864cb7cf",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKGU4ODNhZTY3YjE1OGNkZGQyMzYxZmY2OTY4ZWI2NWM0ODY0Y2I3Y2Y",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-08T00:29:31Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-08T00:29:31Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(motion): judge each pencil of normal lines alone; only inliers vouch for roundness\n\nReview of PR #223 found two more trusted wrong axes from the #208\nmechanism:\n- B1: a prism whose sides are split into 3+ rectangles along its length\n  (square bar, stepped block, stacked cubes) with an off-centre boss read\n  Z through the prism's centre. No one point held half the inliers, so\n  the pencil guard never fired, and the coarseness gate counted the\n  boss's bearings although the boss misses the axis.\n- B2: crossed single-band cylinders read the cross axis: the Z rod's\n  wall is a pencil at the origin that \"meets\" Y, and its union with the\n  Y rod's ring looked round.\n\nThe coarseness gate now reads only the facets that meet the axis. The\ninliers are peeled into pencils (lines through one point, one after\nanother), and each pencil is judged by itself: its area-weighted\ntrigonometric moments k = 1..4 about the axis must vanish (a revolve's\nring is even; a crossing rod piles its share on two bearings, a box on\nfour). The sum, weighted by pencil area, may be at most 10 % of the\ninlier area. A shallow single-band D-flat still reads its axis.\n\nPins (each fails on 2fe41a2):\na_square_bar_split_along_its_length_with_a_boss_is_refused_by_name,\nstepped_and_stacked_blocks_with_a_boss_are_refused_by_name,\ncrossed_cylinders_never_read_the_cross_axis;\na_single_band_shaft_with_a_shallow_flat_still_reads_its_axis guards\nthe D-flat.\n\nFixes #208\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
